], "inputs": [{"name": "text", "link": 4, "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image", "label": "image", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image"}, {"widget": {"name": "output_file_path"}, "name": "output_file_path", "label": "output_file_path", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "output_file_path"}, {"widget": {"name": "file_name"}, "name": "file_name", "label": "file_name", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "file_name"}, {"widget": {"name": "file_extension"}, "name": "file_extension", "label": "file_extension", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "file_extension"}, {"widget": {"name": "overwrite"}, "name": "overwrite", "label": "overwrite", "type": "BOOLEAN", "localized_name": "overwrite"}], "flags": {}, "type": "easy saveText", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#335", "size": [270, 150], "pos": [419.61383056640625, 74.43833923339844], "id": 4, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "easy saveText"}, "order": 7}, {"outputs": [{"name": "STRING", "label": "STRING", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "字符串"}], "color": "#223", "widgets_values": [], "inputs": [{"name": "source", "link": 10, "label": "source", "type": "*", "localized_name": "源"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PreviewAny", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#335", "size": [581.4213256835938, 448.16326904296875], "pos": [817.4544677734375, 74.90377044677734], "id": 13, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PreviewAny"}, "order": 9}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#f4aa14", "widgets_values": ["## -Usage: Package and upload segmented audio of about 5 minutes; then click Run to start training. After training completes, a txt file will be generated. Manually download the trained model via the download link provided in this document.\n## - FAQs:\n## --Q:What is the length of each uploaded 5-minute audio clip? Should it be raw vocal audio of regular speech?\n## --A: The total duration is around 5 minutes; it does not have to be a single continuous clip. Multiple clips can be combined, with each clip ranging from 4 to 15 seconds. All clips must be from the same speaker, raw vocals, and consistent volume. Clean raw vocals mean no BGM, no reverb, and no overlapping voices of multiple people. Normal speaking is acceptable. If you are training for singing, you must use a raw vocal singing dataset for training.\n## --Q:Can Mandarin and Cantonese be mixed in the recordings?\n## A: Yes. The RVC model in this workflow learns timbre instead of language. Mixing Mandarin and Cantonese recordings is allowed, provided all audio is from the same person.\n## --Q:What are the requirements for audio format, compression mode and filenames?\n## A: Standard wav format is sufficient. It is recommended to record audio via Jianying, normalize the volume and remove noise. Export segmented files named s1, s2......Sn, package them into a \".zip\" file, upload it at the node below, and click Run.\nFinally, download the trained model, which is approximately 50–80 MB, and use it in another workflow. You can then cover any song with your voice!\n## After timbre replacement for song covers, whether the output voice resembles the impersonator depends on whether the pitch range provided in the impersonator’s recordings fully covers the pitch range of the target song. Therefore, the voice training set should ideally contain the full pitch range the recorder can produce.\n## -[Conclusion: The criteria for the ideal voice training dataset for song covers are as follows:](1)\n- It does not matter whether the singing sounds good! You only need a sufficient raw vocal singing dataset that covers a wider vocal range with enough high notes.\n- Split the voice training set clips at breath points; each clip should last 4–10 seconds, no shorter than 3 seconds and no longer than 15 seconds.\n- Include low, mid and high pitches, with a total raw singing duration of 5–10 minutes. Both male and female users can record a raw vocal version of Michael Wong's Fairy Tale as the training set, with no accompaniment!\nRecord enough pitch ranges for the voice training set. To reiterate: it does not matter if the singing sounds bad or is out of tune! The priority is to provide enough samples of both high and low pitches.\n- Save training audio in WAV format, 16bit, mono, 40kHz. No transcript text is required.\n- A 5-minute collection of voice training clips, each 4–15 seconds long, usually totals 25–30 clips.\n- Package as \".zip\". None of the filenames can contain Chinese characters."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#e09600", "size": [917.5413208007812, 796.45654296875], "pos": [50.50118637084961, -994.23486328125], "id": 12, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 2}, {"outputs": [{"shape": 6, "name": "图像", "label": "图像", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "图像"}, {"shape": 6, "name": "遮罩", "label": "遮罩", "type": "MASK", "localized_name": "遮罩"}, {"shape": 6, "name": "提示词", "label": "提示词", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "提示词"}, {"shape": 6, "name": "视频", "label": "视频", "type": "VIDEO", "localized_name": "视频"}, {"shape": 6, "name": "音频", "links": [11], "label": "音频", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "音频"}, {"shape": 6, "name": "文本", "label": "文本", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "文本"}, {"name": "命名信息", "label": "命名信息", "type": "*", "localized_name": "命名信息"}], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": [null, null], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "zip_file"}, "name": "zip_file", "label": "zip_file", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "zip_file"}], "flags": {}, "type": "HAIGC_LoadImagesFromZip", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [693.6749267578125, 202], "pos": [-882.8060913085938, -15.486855506896973], "id": 14, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "HAIGC_LoadImagesFromZip"}, "order": 3}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#f4aa14", "widgets_values": ["# [B站 嘉丽有图 Ai教程39](https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1qYnL6tEZo/)\n# [B站 嘉丽有图 Ai教程39 v2 补充教程](https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1Rsnr6fEbS)\n# 有用记得关注我，不断更新更多免费教程！带你遨游ai的海洋，为所欲为~"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#e09600", "size": [1038.0216064453125, 214.0774688720703], "pos": [-498.87835693359375, -1486.4503173828125], "id": 16, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 4}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#f4aa14", "widgets_values": ["# 用法：打包上传约5分钟的分段音频；然后点击运行，开始训练。训练完后生成多个文档，下载最下方那个“demo_rvc_model_pyefp_XXXXXXX.zip\"文档，这就是训练好的你的声音模型了，使用时不需要解压缩！大约60-80mb，下载时间稍微长一点，耐心等待，不要拼命点，会导致反复下载多个！\n# -答疑：\n## --Q:[上传的5分钟的声音，是多长一段？人普通说话的干声吗？](1)\n## --A:合计约 5 分钟，不是必须一整段。可以多段拼起来，每段4到15秒。同一个人、干声、音量一致。干净干声：无BGM、无混响、无多人叠音。正常说话就可以；如果是训练来唱歌，就必须用唱歌的干声训练集来训练。\n\n## --Q:[可以普通话，粤语混合起来说吗？](1)\n## A:可以。本工作流的RVC 模型，学的是音色，不是语言。普通话、粤语混录没问题，必须同一个人\n## --Q:[音频格式？和压缩模式、文件名？](1)\n## A:普通wav即可。推荐用剪映录音，然后把音量统一并去噪。然后分段导出为s1,s2......Sn，然后打包成\".zip\"格式在下面节点上传，点击运行即可。\n#  [最后，下载训练好的模型，大约50-80mb，到另一个工作流里使用，即可用你的声音翻唱一切歌曲!](1)\n## [歌曲翻唱的音色替换后，声音像不像模仿者，取决于模仿者在录音时给出的音高范围是不是完全覆盖了要替换歌曲的音高范围。所以，给出的声音训练集，最好是录制者在其力所能及的范围内的全部音高。](1)\n\n## 结论：最完美的用于翻唱歌曲的声音训练集的标准如下：\n## -唱不唱的好听没关系！给到更多音域范围的足够的高音干声唱歌训练集就行。\n## -声音训练集，每段切在换气处，每段4–10 秒，别短于 3 秒，也别超过 15 秒。\n## -音高要有低、中、高，总长 5–10 分钟的干唱，男女都可以干唱光良的《童话》作为干声训练集，不要有伴奏！以便收集足够的音高范围作为声音训练集。重要的再说一遍：唱不好听，走音跑调都不要紧！最重要的是，给足高低音的样本。\n## -保存的训练集音频格式用 WAV、16bit、单声道、40kHz，不用配文本。\n## -5分钟的声音训练片段集合，每段4-15秒，一般在25-30段。\n## -保存格式为“ .zip”，所有文件命名均不能为中文。"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#e09600", "size": [959.0789184570312, 813.507080078125], "pos": [-1016.3368530273438, -1003.0757446289062], "id": 11, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 1}], "extra": {"links_added_by_ue": [], "ue_links": [], "0246.VERSION": [0, 0, 4], "pixaromaGroups": [], "ds": {"offset": [1315.916092676786, 806.6741288974922], "scale": 1.4122927695244534}}, "groups": [{"color": "#3f789e", "font_size": 24, "flags": {}, "id": 1, "title": "leave me alone", "bounding": [4766.130859375, 3342.214599609375, 608.0